      "note": "Reviewed 2026-09-23: false positive. This MiniRacer eval places a compose or g.script source's syntax error for the refusal the model reads; it runs only after the builder's own compile already refused the source. The text it compiles is the model's source inside a fixed wrapper that begins with `throw 0;`, so V8 parses the whole text and throws before any of it runs: a source that closes the wrapper early is parsed, never executed. It runs in the same fresh V8 context the builder was loaded into, with no attached Ruby callbacks or host IO, under the evaluator's time and memory bounds, and every MiniRacer error it raises is rescued inside the refusal. JavaScript parsing is the refusal's contract, not Ruby eval. Re-review if the wrapper stops leading with the throw, or if the context gains capabilities."
